From: KytyPlus
Subject: Honor SHADPS4_USER_DIR as the highest-priority user-dir override

KytyPlus launches shadPS4 with its working directory set to the shared
parent that already contains a unified `user/` tree, so the portable-dir
detection in path_util.cpp normally adopts it. However, if shadPS4 is ever
run directly from a different cwd (or the portable dir is absent), it falls
back to the platform dir (%APPDATA%/shadPS4 on Windows,
~/.local/share/shadPS4 on Linux), silently splitting saves/settings/caches
and losing the user's sys_modules.

This patch makes shadPS4 honor the SHADPS4_USER_DIR environment variable
as the highest-priority override, so the unified tree is used regardless of
cwd. KytyPlus sets this variable before launching the subprocess.

Context is against shadPS4 v.0.20.0 src/common/path_util.cpp, which indents
with spaces. Regenerate with:
  git diff -- src/common/path_util.cpp > patches/shadps4-user-dir.patch

Apply with:  git apply patches/shadps4-user-dir.patch

--- a/src/common/path_util.cpp
+++ b/src/common/path_util.cpp
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 // SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright 2024-2026 shadPS4 Emulator Project
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
 
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <fstream>
 #include <unordered_map>
 #include "common/logging/log.h"
@@ -88,7 +89,13 @@ static auto UserPaths = [] {
 static auto UserPaths = [] {
     // Try the portable user directory first.
     auto user_dir = std::filesystem::current_path() / PORTABLE_DIR;
-    if (!std::filesystem::exists(user_dir)) {
+    // KytyPlus: honor an explicit override before falling back to the
+    // platform dir. This lets an embedding host pin the unified user tree
+    // even when the portable dir is absent or the cwd differs.
+    if (const char* override_dir = std::getenv("SHADPS4_USER_DIR");
+        override_dir != nullptr && override_dir[0] != '\0') {
+        user_dir = std::filesystem::path(override_dir);
+    } else if (!std::filesystem::exists(user_dir)) {
         // If it doesn't exist, use the standard path for the platform instead.
         // NOTE: On Windows we currently just create the portable directory instead.
 #ifdef __APPLE__
@@ -108,6 +115,9 @@ static auto UserPaths = [] {
 #endif
     }
 
+    // KytyPlus: ensure the override dir exists so create_path() below succeeds.
+    std::filesystem::create_directories(user_dir);
+
     std::unordered_map<PathType, fs::path> paths;
 
     const auto create_path = [&](PathType shad_path, const fs::path& new_path) {
